{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion","id":1541250,"title":"V5 Gehenna War Discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-30T16:34:35-07:00","id":1541250,"title":"V5 Gehenna War Discussion","content":"It's a rather weird book that could use some better writing, especially when there is dialogue between characters and how the Methusalehs are presented. Still going through it, but it really reminds me of Night's Black Agents Double Tap - it's a book about setting up conflict and cool setpieces with vampires mucking about.<br /> <br /> One thing I did not expect, but thought was interesting, is that in addition to the Methusalehs they introduced a number of new factions into the game.<ul><li>Cartographers - Nosferatu Data Brokers</li> <li>Cohort of Wepauwet - Fanatics seeking to purge everyone from the Ministry not belonging to the Church of Set</li> <li>The Dead Lions - Rogue Army seeking to wage war on the Antedelluvians</li> <li>Garrote Vi - Camarilla's hitmen and cleaners that remove any references to the Antedelluvians and Noddism</li> <li>Moon's Army - paramilitary Sabbat organization hunting Salubri and Tremere</li> <li>Servitors of Irad - Servitors of the Antedlluvians</li> <li>Shepherds of Ur-Shulgi - Agents of Ur-Shulgi</li> <li>the Boule - Independant Dealers in Lore and Money</li> <li>Circulatory System Borard of Trust - Enforcers of the Circulatory System</li> <li>Los Hijos de Si - Peruan Blood Cult</li> <li>Mora's Death Seers - Harbingers of Skulls that did not drop their grudge</li> <li>Oradea League - Kindred Illuminati that seeks to be the new Camarilla</li> <li>Oswobodocziele (Liberators) - Ghoul liberation insurrection</li> <li>Throne's Keepers - Vampires that run Kosovo (really Renegade... REALLY?)</li> </ul>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T02:24:37-07:00","id":1541275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion#post1541250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Throne's Keepers - Vampires that run Kosovo (really Renegade... REALLY?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere it's implied they run Kosovo, though, Just that they are the dominant Vampire faction in Kosovo and try to keep Gehenna crusaders away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T02:33:29-07:00","id":1541278,"title":"","content":"I'd Say that GEHENNA WAR Is a must have supplement, along with the Players Guide.<br /> <br /> It has<br /> <br /> - 10 new faction<br /> - rules for Elders and Methuselahs in the V5 framework<br /> - a recap of combat with many new useful options that eschew the risk of creating strange subsystems and are instrad refinements of the main rules<br /> - loads of discipline Powers<br /> - Teo very informative and well written chapters on how to run action and action horror chronicles<br /> <br /> And above all a chapter on when and how to roll in game, how ti adjust dice modes to different narrarions, Messy Criticala and Bestiale Failures tables tailored on Skills, and many other goodies that are basically a guide to the narrative flow of v5<br /> <br /> There are also 7 Methuselahs and some Infos on Beckoning, even though they are still in the &quot;plot hooks which gi\u00f9 Will build on&quot; mode, no hard truths or huge lore dumps.<br /> <br /> The 4 mini Chronicles are also fun and full of tongue in cheek jokes (an Assamite Battle Royale in a Chiese restaurante!)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T02:40:38-07:00","id":1541279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541275#post1541275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nowhere it's implied they run Kosovo, though, Just that they are the dominant Vampire faction in Kosovo and try to keep Gehenna crusaders away.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are a cult based on this: <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goddess_on_the_Throne\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goddess_on_the_Throne</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T07:52:25-07:00","id":1541285,"title":"","content":"I haven't gotten hands-on with the PDF yet, but I will say the changes I definitely like from what I've heard are:<br /> <br /> - Hard-set rules for enhanced BP via simply drinking methuselah vitae.<br /> <br /> - Elder-level disciplines as advantage modifiers to existing powers.<br /> <br /> - The implications of V5 bloodform make the acidic blood/bloodform combo from past editions look bush league.<br /> <br /> - Rules for brutal attacking look pretty nice. I had actually started work on a house rule for this exact thing, and it's nice to see just published.<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% sure about the need for umpteen new subfactions, but on the other hand it's nice to get more information on the subfactions that already existed and/or have been hinted at already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T12:40:59-07:00","id":1541302,"title":"","content":"I can't wait to check it out if nothing else for ideas of amalgam powers that I haven't thought about yet. Esspecially when it comes with Obfuscate, Auspex and Presence or Fortitude combos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T19:33:03-07:00","id":1541317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541278#post1541278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd Say that GEHENNA WAR Is a must have supplement, along with the Players Guide.<br /> <br /> It has<br /> <br /> - 10 new faction<br /> - rules for Elders and Methuselahs in the V5 framework<br /> - a recap of combat with many new useful options that eschew the risk of creating strange subsystems and are instrad refinements of the main rules<br /> - loads of discipline Powers<br /> - Teo very informative and well written chapters on how to run action and action horror chronicles<br /> <br /> And above all a chapter on when and how to roll in game, how ti adjust dice modes to different narrarions, Messy Criticala and Bestiale Failures tables tailored on Skills, and many other goodies that are basically a guide to the narrative flow of v5<br /> <br /> There are also 7 Methuselahs and some Infos on Beckoning, even though they are still in the &quot;plot hooks which gi\u00f9 Will build on&quot; mode, no hard truths or huge lore dumps.<br /> <br /> The 4 mini Chronicles are also fun and full of tongue in cheek jokes (an Assamite Battle Royale in a Chiese restaurante!)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Elders rules? Yup I just bought it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T20:17:14-07:00","id":1541319,"title":"","content":"Cohort of Wepauwet, Oradea League, and Servitors of Irad aren't particularly new. Why the Oradea League would want to become the &quot;new Camarilla&quot; is beyond me, because they've always just been a league of Tzimisce elders that eschewed Vissicitude and tried to rule the old ways. Of the Methuselahs in the book (Tiamat, Ur-shulgi, Enkidu, Kemintiri, Plague-Bride, Shalim, and Ceri) only Shalim and Ceri are new and both of which has descriptions trying to imply they are something other than kindred. The Methuselah powers are all &quot;hey look I win&quot; buttons without any real rules. For example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Unavoidable Hunter (Celerity): So fast they appear to require no effort at all to move, the methuselah is always where they need to be. They're impossible to hit and may always be right behind you. After activating this power, the methuselah may always choose to be where they want to be within a hundred-meter radius. They can evade any attack that targets their person and they can always reach any enemy. They can still be affected by broad area-of-effect attacks, such as the collapsing of an entire building&quot; </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Ok. Whatever. The others are mostly the same sort of flavors of stupid. The rest of the book is likewise pretty meh, like the rest of V5 has been. I'd be disappointed, if I had any disappointment left for V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T02:29:41-07:00","id":1541325,"title":"","content":"A lot of neat ideas although moons army seems a bit redundant with the Black hand as an already established faction with greater depth and range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T03:32:38-07:00","id":1541326,"title":"","content":"I am very confused why they made Legacy non-canon and then release a bunch of stuff that had already been developed by Onyx Path. This reads like it was mostly taken from Blood Cults.<br /> <br /> Which isn't a bad thing because Blood Cults is the 2nd best thing for 5th Edition but its confusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T06:36:19-07:00","id":1541331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541326#post1541326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very confused why they made Legacy non-canon and then release a bunch of stuff that had already been developed by Onyx Path. This reads like it was mostly taken from Blood Cults.<br /> <br /> Which isn't a bad thing because Blood Cults is the 2nd best thing for 5th Edition but its confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think thats it really, the oynx path stuff was well received. I also think theyve written themselves into a corner in terms of supplementry works. No paths, no unique disciplines, downplays sect culture, clans are archeotypes not cultures etc this leaves the cults outside of clan lores as one of the few outlets if you want to be creative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T08:00:43-07:00","id":1541333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541326#post1541326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very confused why they made Legacy non-canon and then release a bunch of stuff that had already been developed by Onyx Path. This reads like it was mostly taken from Blood Cults.<br /> <br /> Which isn't a bad thing because Blood Cults is the 2nd best thing for 5th Edition but its confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cults is not Legacy nor a property of OPP. They also never said &quot;Legacy Will be thrown in a bin&quot;: V5 Is a continuation with the freedom of updating or retconning things.<br /> <br /> That they have thrown away everything and then are using Legacy ideas out of desperation Is Just a talking point of WOD5 enemies, but has never bene true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T08:02:33-07:00","id":1541334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541331#post1541331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think thats it really, the oynx path stuff was well received. I also think theyve written themselves into a corner in terms of supplementry works. No paths, no unique disciplines, downplays sect culture, clans are archeotypes not cultures etc this leaves the cults outside of clan lores as one of the few outlets if you want to be creative.</div> </div> </div> </div>In every supplement which has come out so far there are new Powers, Merita, Flaws and Loresheets, as well as new cults or faction within the other sects (Moon's Army Is a Sabbat faction).<br /> <br /> They do not look that much into a corner, to me \ud83d\ude05","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":".  Grammar 09-01-2024, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T08:14:41-07:00","id":1541336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541333#post1541333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cults is not Legacy nor a property of OPP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and?<br /> <br /> It's also built heavily from previous lore, which they've made it clear they're ambivalent about. It's not an insult, just an observation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T08:25:52-07:00","id":1541337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541336#post1541336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, and?<br /> <br /> It's also built heavily from previous lore, which they've made it clear they're ambivalent about. It's not an insult, just an observation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, It came out harsher than I meant it.<br /> <br /> That said, they never stated they were never gonna touch old lore again, only that they were not bound by It.<br /> <br /> It's good and sound strategy that they go forward with plot points established in Cults, it's not a source book from a separate line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-01-2024, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T08:55:07-07:00","id":1541339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541334#post1541334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In every supplement which has come out so far there are new Powers, Merita, Flaws and Loresheets, as well as new cults or faction within the other sects (Moon's Army Is a Sabbat faction).<br /> <br /> They do not look that much into a corner, to me \ud83d\ude05</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sort of my point they can only really write about certain things, they can't do much with the Sabbat so they do small weird cults, they can't do bloodlines or clan deep dives so they churn out loresheets<br /> <br /> The moons army highlights this issue as the Black hand are comparatively going to have a lot more ink spilt on them which highlights my point very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T10:25:16-07:00","id":1541341,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not like they cannot writer about things, they write about them differently.<br /> <br /> Deep lore dives are not in the style of the edition: actionable plot hooks, Loresheets and subfactions are the tools they use now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T10:35:42-07:00","id":1541342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541341#post1541341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's not like they cannot writer about things, they write about them differently.<br /> <br /> Deep lore dives are not in the style of the edition: actionable plot hooks, Loresheets and subfactions are the tools they use now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and thats exactly my point. They cant really write about what they used to so now we get a lot of blood god style stuff.<br /> you cant do black hand so you do moons army. You cant do sabbat so you do church caine.<br /> <br /> Which is 'fine' but it does raise the question of simply cutting the knot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-01-2024, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T11:52:36-07:00","id":1541343,"title":"","content":"I'm unlikely to read the book admittedly, but seeing Los Hijos de Si included is interesting, as we were required to cut most of the text from that section in Cults of the Blood Gods. It makes me wonder if that text has now been repurposed for Gehenna War and if so whether the authors went uncredited again as we did when our work was reprinted in the Players Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T11:54:04-07:00","id":1541344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541342#post1541342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and thats exactly my point. They cant really write about what they used to so now we get a lot of blood god style stuff.<br /> you cant do black hand so you do moons army. You cant do sabbat so you do church caine.<br /> <br /> Which is 'fine' but it does raise the question of simply cutting the knot.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Gehenna War has a fair chunk of the book committed to the Sabbat , and the Moon's s Army is thematically totally different from the Black Hand. It's connected to the Classic Saulot / Tremere / Goratrix shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T12:12:52-07:00","id":1541347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541343#post1541343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unlikely to read the book admittedly, but seeing Los Hijos de Si included is interesting, as we were required to cut most of the text from that section in Cults of the Blood Gods. It makes me wonder if that text has now been repurposed for Gehenna War and if so whether the authors went uncredited again as we did when our work was reprinted in the Players Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>The text doesn't add anything new, however It has a distinct Drowned Legacies feeling.<br /> <br /> The credited writers are <br /> <br /> WRITERS: Rachel J. Wilkinson, Jose Garcia with Juhana Pettersson, Kevin Schluter &amp; Jukka S\u00e4rkij\u00e4rvi<br /> <br /> Hope they did their credits right \ud83e\udd1e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T12:21:59-07:00","id":1541348,"title":"","content":"So it's just reprinted from Cults of the Blood Gods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T12:49:01-07:00","id":1541350,"title":"","content":"I'd say summarized, it's way shorter than the Cults' writeup, and with less details (no suggested Convinctions for instance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T13:03:03-07:00","id":1541352,"title":"","content":"I haven't yet read Gehenna War. Is it like what they did with the Howl section in Shattered Nation?<br /> <br /> This is W20:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chant of Challenge \u2014 This howl begins like the Howl of Introduction, then rolls into a vicious mockery of an enemy\u2019s deeds, ancestry and personal habits. The Fianna invented this howl as a method of initiating duels, then later elevated it to a satirical art form. Everyone hearing the chant can discern exactly why the challenge is taking place. </div> </div> </div>And this is what they put into W5 Shattered Nation:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chant of Challenge: A howl that begins as the Howl of Introduction but then switches into a mockery of an enemy\u2019s deeds, personal habits, and ancestry. It is meant to initiate a duel, and every Garou hearing it understands the precise reasons for the challenge. Among Hart Wardens, the Chant of Challenge has been elevated into a satirical art form.\u200b </div> </div> </div>It's like when you're in highschool and you're copying someone else's homework but you're haphazardly trying to hide it. Are they doing something like that in Gehenna War as well with Cult of the Blood Gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T13:50:19-07:00","id":1541355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541352#post1541352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't yet read Gehenna War. Is it like what they did with the Howl section in Shattered Nation?<br /> <br /> This is W20:<br /> <br /> <br /> And this is what they put into W5 Shattered Nation:<br /> <br /> <br /> It's like when you're in highschool and you're copying someone else's homework but you're haphazardly trying to hide it. Are they doing something like that in Gehenna War as well with Cult of the Blood Gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Elder powers are basically that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T19:43:02-07:00","id":1541376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion#post1541250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oradea League - Kindred Illuminati that seeks to be the new Camarilla</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooo! I didn't know they were slated to get any more of a write-up. I'll probably have to buy this book, as my main character was a prospective member and deeply involved in their goings-on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T22:23:42-07:00","id":1541380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541352#post1541352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't yet read Gehenna War. Is it like what they did with the Howl section in Shattered Nation?<br /> <br /> This is W20:<br /> <br /> <br /> And this is what they put into W5 Shattered Nation:<br /> <br /> <br /> It's like when you're in highschool and you're copying someone else's homework but you're haphazardly trying to hide it. Are they doing something like that in Gehenna War as well with Cult of the Blood Gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should it be surprising that they used the same text for a Power that Is just the same but mechanically translated? It's two edition of the same game, from the same IP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T22:59:43-07:00","id":1541381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541380#post1541380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why should it be surprising that they used the same text for a Power that Is just the same but mechanically translated? It's two edition of the same game, from the same IP.</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It would almost be easier to stomach if they had just used the same text. Then at least it would simply be a copy-paste-job. Instead, someone took it upon themselves to recreate another writer's work by slightly rearranging what is said when and using slightly different language with the same connotation.</li> <li>The original writer should be credited when the copy-pasting and obvious lack of creativity on the new writer's part is this blatant. All they needed to do was carve out a section on the credits page to own up to the fact that they clearly were copy-pasting writing from the W20 corebook. Simply giving credit where it's due.</li> <li>An obvious and easy fix would've been to take this WtA-concept and write something entirely original. Here's an idea from me: Take that entire section, look to W20 but then make the angle &quot;Then and Now&quot;. The W5 setting is supposed to be different anyway. Age of Apocalypse, fallen Garou-Nation, Septs constantly being at each other's throat: Just take that and describe how the meaning of these Howls has changed. That way you're conceptually writing something else from the outset other than just slavishly reproducing something from the W20 corebook. If you're doing the latter, the decent thing to do is just honor the original work you took that stuff from...</li> <li>In the case of W5, the whole premise was supposed to be &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;. The intent was very much not to repeat/continue ideas from previous editions. So maybe they should do that then rather than pilfering previous work, right?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T04:27:49-07:00","id":1541388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541376#post1541376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooooo! I didn't know they were slated to get any more of a write-up. I'll probably have to buy this book, as my main character was a prospective member and deeply involved in their goings-on.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's maybe two pages. So keep that in mind if it's the only reason to get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T09:18:36-07:00","id":1541393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541381#post1541381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It would almost be easier to stomach if they had just used the same text. Then at least it would simply be a copy-paste-job. Instead, someone took it upon themselves to recreate another writer's work by slightly rearranging what is said when and using slightly different language with the same connotation.</li> <li>The original writer should be credited when the copy-pasting and obvious lack of creativity on the new writer's part is this blatant. All they needed to do was carve out a section on the credits page to own up to the fact that they clearly were copy-pasting writing from the W20 corebook. Simply giving credit where it's due.</li> <li>An obvious and easy fix would've been to take this WtA-concept and write something entirely original. Here's an idea from me: Take that entire section, look to W20 but then make the angle &quot;Then and Now&quot;. The W5 setting is supposed to be different anyway. Age of Apocalypse, fallen Garou-Nation, Septs constantly being at each other's throat: Just take that and describe how the meaning of these Howls has changed. That way you're conceptually writing something else from the outset other than just slavishly reproducing something from the W20 corebook. If you're doing the latter, the decent thing to do is just honor the original work you took that stuff from...</li> <li>In the case of W5, the whole premise was supposed to be &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;. The intent was very much not to repeat/continue ideas from previous editions. So maybe they should do that then rather than pilfering previous work, right?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>What you are asking for Is for Wod5e to Say &quot;so, we are a completely different, unrelated things, and in case we use something from Legacy, we must stress its uniqueness and implied superiority&quot;. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bBut they never said this was going to be the case, and it's perfectly normale: V5 Is a liberal continuation, W5 a re imagination, and nowhere they implied they were gonna cut every Legacy aspect, only that they kept themselves the option to use It or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T09:19:25-07:00","id":1541394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541388#post1541388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's maybe two pages. So keep that in mind if it's the only reason to get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also there isn't honestly much new from them in the writeup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T09:48:09-07:00","id":1541396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541250-v5-gehenna-war-discussion?p=1541393#post1541393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you are asking for Is for Wod5e to Say &quot;so, we are a completely different, unrelated things, and in case we use something from Legacy, we must stress its uniqueness and implied superiority&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200bBut they never said this was going to be the case, and it's perfectly normale: V5 Is a liberal continuation, W5 a re imagination, and nowhere they implied they were gonna cut every Legacy aspect, only that they kept themselves the option to use It or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your descriptions of &quot;so, we are a completely different, unrelated things, and in case we use something from Legacy, we must stress its uniqueness and implied superiority&quot; is a perfect description of the mission-statement of W5. That's why three Tribes got renamed, that's why the setting has a fallen Garou-Nation, why sweeping setting-changes have been introduced like Gaia being dead/dying, the Get of Fenris Tribe being turned into a fallen Tribe, Kinfolk getting removed etc. Everything points to one of the goals of W5 being that it's supposed to be <i>very different</i>. How well it does on that point is a whole other question. And you're missing one important part of the quote from that sidebar at the beginning. And I think this might explain your confusion on this point. The phrase is that it's a &quot;re-imagination, <b>not a continuation</b>.&quot;. So if you're taking a piece from W20 and you're just copy-pasting things... well, then clearly there isn't a lot of re-imagining going on while indicating that it's obviously a continuation.<br /> <br /> Besides, the central issue is that this is about taking work from other writers and putting it into these two supplements without the people working on the new supplements adding any new original material to these copied sections. And then the books leave the original writers whose work was copied uncredited. So in the case, I quoted above, nobody on that writing-team ever worked on that Howl-section in Shattered Nation. Somebody just took their copy of the W20 corebook, went to the section on Howls and started copy-pasting that stuff while doing some light reshuffling with the words to not make it too obvious. A professional should be able to do better than that.<br /> <br /> And like I said at the beginning, W5 starts with &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;. So W5 had the full license to do new things and to do things differently. To take that and then just copy-paste stuff from W20. And then you're not even crediting the original writers you took this stuff from...? That's just indecent and lazy on top of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T15:15:34-07:00","id":1541488,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Asmodai;n1541250]It's a rather weird book that could use some better writing, especially when there is dialogue between characters and how the Methusalehs are presented. Still going through it, but it really reminds me of Night's Black Agents Double Tap - it's a book about setting up conflict and cool setpieces with vampires mucking about.<br /> <br /> One thing I did not expect, but thought was interesting, is that in addition to the Methusalehs they introduced a number of new factions into the game.[LIST][*]Cartographers - Nosferatu Data Brokers <br /> This sounds like a good faction to learn more about and maybe adapt to our game.[*]Cohort of Wepauwet - Fanatics seeking to purge everyone from the Ministry not belonging to the Church of Set<br /> <br /> This has some potential, but can't see us using it to any great extent.[*]The Dead Lions - Rogue Army seeking to wage war on the Antedelluvians<br /> <br /> This would fit with our idea of rogue war packs who can't see themselves as anything but what they are.<br /> <br /> [[*]Servitors of Irad - Servitors of the Antedlluvians<br /> <br /> Having some form of Manus Igrim should work in small doses.[*]Shepherds of Ur-Shulgi - Agents of Ur-Shulgi<br /> <br /> Admittedly I'm not a big fan of this ancient monster and I don't want much to do with him in general.[*]the Boule - Independant Dealers in Lore and Money<br /> <br /> This sounds okay, but wouldn't they be stepping on a lot of factions who are in the same business?[*]Circulatory System Borard of Trust - Enforcers of the Circulatory System<br /> <br /> This makes sense that the Circulatory System would need muscle to protect there interests.<br /> [<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T05:46:23-07:00","id":1541525,"title":"","content":"<br /> The changes in terms of mechanics are very very big, especially in terms of elder and matusalem powers. In addition to big mechanical changes there are also some radical changes in terms of V5 lore.<br /> <br /> 1) Gehenna War is no longer limited to war zones or the Middle East. It is a global conflict that is also happening in Europe and America and throughout Asia, including Singapore<br /> <br /> 2) Enkidu is alive and is in Poland (in V20 he was said to have been killed outside Prague)<br /> <br /> 3) Francois Villon had the Sarcophagus of Tiamat brought to Paris, and now the Methuselah is free in Europe<br /> <br /> 4) Not only is Ur-Shulgi is fine, but Izhim ur-Baal has joined him and now leads the Shepherds of Ur-Shulgi. I would say that this connection further reinforces the theory that Ur-Shulgi is not only the third Baali founder, but continues to play for them.<br /> <br /> 5) Unre did not receive the cease-fire memo after the Family Reunion and continues to hunt the Giovanni through an organization known as Mora's Death Seers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T19:46:04-07:00","id":1541559,"title":"","content":"I wondered what happened to Unre and how she reacted to the events of the Last Supper and figured that maybe Lazarus quietly eliminated her and what the eldest Grand childe of Haqim was up to since the breaking of the clan curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T14:51:17-07:00","id":1541751,"title":"","content":"I thought Unre was Constancia, and thus her current circumstances were dealt with in <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T15:57:34-07:00","id":1541754,"title":"","content":"I always figured that Unre and Lady Constancia were seperate childer of Japeth myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.c